## Build brief

**Concept — "the front desk."** The page is ordered the way a person asks at the door: *can I be seen today → will you turn me away → what can you treat → how do I get there → will anyone understand me → do I need to book.* Sections: 911 strip, masthead, live status, assurances, services, getting here, languages, booking, footer.

**Signature component — the week bar with a live now-line.** All seven days plotted against a shared 7:00–21:00 axis, so the shape of the week (long Mon–Thu, short Fri, half-day Sat, closed Sun) reads in one glance, with every time also printed. Today's column is outlined and carries a `NOW` marker at the real current time.

The status headline is **derived, not hardcoded**: it computes open / registration-closed / opens-later / closed-today from the clock and the hours table, using the clinic's own stated rule that registration closes 30 minutes before the doors. During Monday opening hours it reads exactly *"Open now for walk-ins — Last patient accepted at 19:30 today."* At other times it says the true thing instead. A fact line (`Today, Monday · 8:00–20:00 · registration until 19:30`) is present in **every** state so the required hours are never inferred from the headline. Colour carries the state: green open, amber registration-closed, slate closed.

**Visual system.** Warm recycled-paper ground, deep ink-green, one signal red reserved entirely for the 911 notice — green never decorates, it means open/free/go. Bricolage Grotesque for the few things read from across a room, Public Sans (the US civic interface face) for everything else, tabular figures throughout since the page is mostly times. Icons from Lucide (ISC), sized by role. No photography: this clinic is fictional, so stock exteriors or a map of 1140 East Barrow Street would be a fabricated claim rather than a placeholder — that's a deliberate omission, not a skipped hunt.

**Other decisions.** Services are split by the only axis that changes what you do next — five walk-in, one book-ahead — as a ledger with cost right-aligned, not a table of prose or a six-card grid. The assurances are the page's one full-bleed break, set at 40px on saturated green. Mobile replaces the seven-column plot with seven rows rather than shrinking it.

**Motion.** Interaction baseline everywhere (hover, focus-visible, press, one grammar); bars grow on load, the registration-window rule fills, regions enter against the top of the viewport, once. Reduced motion verified: 0 sections left hidden.

